### Step 5 — Snapshot manager (time-travel)

**Files:** `cli/snapshots/snapshots.go`, `cli/snapshots/restore.go`

**On `agentops dev` start:**
```go
func InitSession(sessionID, workDir string) error {
    // 1. Run `git status` — if in a git repo, note current HEAD
    // 2. Create snapshot dir: ~/.agentops/snapshots/<session_id>/
    // 3. Take initial snapshot (snapshot_000)
    // 4. Start periodic ticker: every 60s → TakeSnapshot()
}
```

**Taking a snapshot:**
```go
func TakeSnapshot(sessionID, workDir, trigger string) (snapshotID string, err error) {
    // 1. Run `git diff HEAD` — save full diff as patch file
    // 2. List untracked files (`git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`)
    // 3. Copy untracked files verbatim into snapshot dir
    // 4. Record manifest: { timestamp, git_head, patch_file, untracked_files[] }
    // 5. Insert into snapshots table
}
```

**Restoring:**
```go
func Restore(sessionID, snapshotID, workDir string) error {
    // 1. Load snapshot manifest
    // 2. `git checkout HEAD -- .`  (reset tracked files)
    // 3. `git apply <patch_file>`  (re-apply changes up to snapshot point)
    // 4. Copy untracked files back from snapshot dir
    // 5. Print: "✓ Restored to <timestamp>. <N> files changed."
}
```

**CLI (`cmd/restore.go`):**
```
agentops restore                          # list recent sessions with snapshot counts
agentops restore <run_id>                 # list snapshots for that session
agentops restore <run_id> --at <ts>       # restore to closest snapshot before <ts>
agentops restore <run_id> --snapshot <id> # restore to exact snapshot
agentops restore --dry-run                # show what would change, don't apply
```

Dashboard: every event row in trace detail has a "↩ Restore to here" button that
calls `POST /api/restore { session_id, snapshot_id }`.

