**New pages beyond original spec:**

**`/blame` — AI Diff Attribution**
- Left panel: file tree of all files touched this session
- Right panel: click a file → timeline of every AI edit
  - Each row: timestamp, agent badge, +N/-N lines, expandable diff
  - Diff rendered with `react-diff-view` or similar
- Search/filter by agent, date range

**`/mcp` — MCP Server Health**
- Table: server name, status dot (green/amber/red), call count, error rate, avg latency, p95 latency
- Click a server → call history chart (latency over time), recent errors
- Alert badges inline: "⚠ p95 > 2s", "✗ error rate 15%"

**`/prompts` — Prompt Versions**
- Table: hash (first 8 chars), first seen, sessions, avg cost, avg tokens, avg efficiency score
- Click → full prompt text (scrubbed), list of sessions using it
- "Compare" button: select two → side-by-side unified diff

**Budget banner (global, in layout.tsx):**
```
When spend > 80% of limit:
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ⚠ Budget  $1.67 / $2.00 (84%)  ·  43 / 50 tools    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
amber background, dismissible per session
```

**Efficiency badge (on all LLM call events):**
- Green circle: score ≥ 70
- Amber circle: 40–69
- Red circle: < 40
- Tooltip: "1,200 of 8,400 prompt tokens referenced in output"

**Trace detail — restore button:**
Each event row in the timeline has a hover action:
```
[↩ Restore to here]  — calls POST /api/restore
```
Shows confirmation modal: "This will reset your working directory to <timestamp>. Continue?"

