## Key Implementation Notes

### Go module
```
module github.com/agentops-dev/agentops
go 1.22
```

### Go dependencies
```
github.com/spf13/cobra              # CLI
github.com/marcboeker/go-duckdb     # DuckDB
github.com/fsnotify/fsnotify        # fs watching
github.com/oklog/ulid/v2            # ULIDs
github.com/rs/zerolog               # logging
github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2         # HTTP server
github.com/sergi/go-diff/diffmatchpatch  # prompt diffing
crypto/sha256                       # prompt hashing (stdlib)
```

### Config file `~/.agentops/config.json`
```json
{
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "session_id": "<ulid>",
  "detected_tools": ["claude", "cursor", "shell"],
  "proxy_port": 4318,
  "collector_port": 4317,
  "hooks_installed": true,
  "data_dir": "~/.agentops/data",
  "snapshots_dir": "~/.agentops/snapshots",
  "scrub_patterns_file": "~/.agentops/scrub_patterns.txt",
  "budget": {
    "cost_limit_usd": 2.00,
    "tool_call_limit": 50,
    "action": "pause"
  }
}
```

### Collector concurrency model
```go
type Collector struct {
    events   chan Event     // buffered, size 512
    store    *store.Store
    scrubber *scrubber.Scrubber
    budget   *budget.Checker
    alerts   *alerts.Engine
    done     chan struct{}
}

// Single writer goroutine — all events flow through here
func (c *Collector) writeLoop() {
    for e := range c.events {
        scrubbed := c.scrubber.ScrubEvent(&e)
        c.store.WriteEvent(scrubbed)
        c.budget.Check(scrubbed.SessionID)
        c.alerts.Check(scrubbed)
        c.broadcast(scrubbed)  // SSE
    }
}
```

### Error handling
- Never panic in daemon. Log and continue.
- DuckDB write failure: buffer in ring buffer (max 1000), retry with backoff
- Proxy upstream failure: pass error through to caller, still log event with `Error` field set
- Scrubber failure: log error, store event with all string fields replaced by `[SCRUB_ERROR]`
- Snapshot failure: log, continue — never block the main collector

### Testing
- `scrubber_test.go`: test every pattern against real-looking fake secrets
- `efficiency_test.go`: test scorer against known prompt/output pairs
- `budget_test.go`: seed DuckDB with events, verify violations trigger correctly
- `proxy_test.go`: integration test with mock upstream
- `detector/*_test.go`: mock filesystem per tool
- Dashboard: Playwright E2E for blame page and restore confirmation flow (v0.2)

---

## Environment Variables

```bash
AGENTOPS_DATA_DIR           # override ~/.agentops/data
AGENTOPS_PORT               # override 4318
AGENTOPS_LOG_LEVEL          # debug|info|warn|error
AGENTOPS_NO_BROWSER         # =1 skip auto-open
AGENTOPS_REDACT_CONTENT     # =1 redact all prompt/output text (keep only metadata)
AGENTOPS_NO_SNAPSHOTS       # =1 disable time-travel snapshots
AGENTOPS_BUDGET_COST        # override budget cost limit (float)
AGENTOPS_BUDGET_ACTION      # override budget action: alert|pause|kill
OPENAI_BASE_URL             # set by agentops init → proxy
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL          # set by agentops init → proxy
```

---

## What NOT to Build in v0.1

- Cloud sync or team features
- `agentops eval` (v0.2)
- Multi-agent conflict detection (v0.3)
- Prompt governance / approval workflows (v0.3)
- Any authentication
- AI-powered smart callouts (v0.2)

The scrubber, budget daemon, and snapshot manager ARE v0.1 — do not defer them.

---

## Definition of Done for v0.1

- [ ] `agentops init` completes in < 3s, detects tools, reports privacy filter active
- [ ] `agentops dev` starts daemon + opens dashboard without errors
- [ ] OpenAI proxy intercepts, scrubs, and records LLM calls accurately
- [ ] Scrubber strips all 8 built-in secret patterns from test inputs
- [ ] Shell hook records commands + exit codes
- [ ] Filesystem watcher records file edits + inserts attribution rows
- [ ] Budget daemon triggers alert at 80%, correct action (pause/kill/alert) at 100%
- [ ] Snapshot taken on session start; `agentops restore` lists snapshots and applies correctly
- [ ] Prompt hash captured per LLM call; `agentops prompt list` shows versions
- [ ] MCP calls recorded with latency; `/mcp` page shows per-server health
- [ ] Efficiency score computed and stored on every LLM call event
- [ ] Live feed shows events < 500ms latency
- [ ] Budget banner appears in dashboard when > 80% of limit
- [ ] Trace detail "Restore to here" button works end-to-end
- [ ] Daemon < 50MB RSS under normal load
- [ ] No events dropped at 100 events/second sustained
- [ ] Dashboard loads < 1s on localhost
- [ ] Works on macOS arm64, macOS x86, Linux x86_64
